Subject: [PATCH] Withholding check: simple first, and what to write on your
 W-4 or W-4P

Gap #30 (P4, P3) with the page's simple-first conversion (opt C12). The page opens
with the answer, its sentence and one filled button; the four figures, the paycheck
boxes and how the W-4 works are quiet rows one tap away, and "More on this" links
the Paycheck and Estimated payments pages. An outlined "Print what to write" draws
the form line by line and prints it: Step 4(c) is the page's own figure, the 2(c)
box is checked only for two jobs, Step 3 says the children's amount (2,200 a child
under 17, 500 another dependent, from the 2026 forms read on irs.gov today). For a
pension it is the W-4P, one per pension, with its "No withholding" box, and the
page says W-4P and "payment". No line for a Social Security number.

compute() and every function the other pages read are byte-identical to bd8595f
over 1,408 qa household plans and the fixtures (25,610 comparisons). The first-view
entry only goes down: 390 words, 14 figures, 4 boxes and 2 filled buttons become
190 words (the empty plan's 160 words drop under its budget).

